>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `export_refute_simp`

``` hol4
Refute.export_refute_simp : string -> unit
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Adds a theorem to the equations the model finder uses.

`export_refute_simp name` adds the theorem `name` to the theory's
`refute_simp` set, which persists with the theory.  The model finder
uses each conjunct of the theorem as an equation for the constant
heading it.  Each conjunct must be `c t1 ... tn = u`, `c t1 ... tn` or
`~(c t1 ... tn)` for a constant `c`; the model finder drops any other
conjunct with a warning.

### Comments

The theorem attribute `refute_simp` has the same effect.

